        id: "agreement-partial-recon-fixed",
        document: "agreement",
        section: "New Section 7 (before Borrower’s Warranties)",
        mode: "append subsection",
        template: "7. Partial Release and Reconveyance.\n(a) Any one or all of the parcels of the Real Property described in the Deed of Trust (each, a Parcel) may be released from the lien of the Deed of Trust and reconveyed prior to the payment of all obligations evidenced by the Note and the Deed of Trust, only when each and all of the following conditions precedent to such partial release are fully performed and met.\n(i) Borrower is not in default under the Loan Documents in the payment of principal, interest, taxes, insurance premiums, loan costs, or fees, or in the performance of any of the terms, conditions, or covenants of the Note and the Deed of Trust;\n(ii) No event has occurred which, after notice, passage of time, or both, shall constitute a default;\n(iii) All real property security for the payment of the Note and other indebtedness described in the Deed of Trust, other than portions of the real property security, if any, previously reconveyed pursuant hereto, and portions of the real property that may now be released as provided herein, is and shall remain subject to the lien of the Deed of Trust;\n(iv) Borrower shall have paid all costs, trustee's fees, attorneys’ fees if incurred by Lender, and expenses of Lender incurred in connection with any reconveyance;\n(v) Lender shall receive, at Borrower's expense, a CLTA Endorsement No. 111 to its policy of title insurance obtained upon making the Loan secured hereby, as well as any other title endorsements reasonably required by Lender;\n(vi) The consideration for the partial release and reconveyance of any one or all of the subject Parcels shall be {{parcel_one_amount}} for Parcel 1 and {{parcel_two_amount}} for Parcel 2. The consideration received by Lender for such partial release shall be applied to reduce the unpaid principal balance of the Note. No consideration for a partial release shall affect the due date of subsequent installments of principal and/or interest; and\n(b) When each and all of the foregoing six (6) conditions shall have been performed and met, the subject Parcel shall be released and Lender shall execute a Request for Reconveyance directing the Trustee to reconvey such Parcel. Additionally, Lender shall execute such documents, instruments and agreements necessary to accomplish or effectuate the terms of this section.",
